A failable cleanup is acquired, then a later provider can fail. If it does, the
mid-build unwind runs the acquired cleanup, captures its error, and joins it with
the build error via errors.Join. The success path has a lone failable cleanup, so
it returns that error directly: errors.Join (and the errors import) come only
from the unwind.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type A struct{}
type B struct{}

//plumb:build
func OpenA() (*A, func() error) { return &A{}, func() error { return nil } }

//plumb:build
func OpenB(a *A) (*B, error) { return &B{}, nil }
